Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

Complaint status alone may overstate resolution when the same customer return=
s, the transaction remains unresolved or the account closes. The possible sto=
ries are that resolved complaints do not recur, that specific categories lead=
 to repeat contact or attrition, or that resolution notes are generic.

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use November 2024 as the new evidence point rath=
er than recycling the earlier conclusion. Please start with the decision we n=
eed to make, then show whether the available evidence is strong enough to sup=
port it.

Please prepare a Power BI page with drill-through to a reproducible case list=
. The output must help us decide which complaint outcomes need quality review=
 and which root causes need fixing.

Data available: customer contacts, complaints and suggestions; transaction-le=
vel timestamps, channels, amounts, statuses and error context; monthly accoun=
t snapshots, status events, limits, product enrolments and signatories.

Please state the limitation plainly: The analysis can identify recurrence and=
 later behaviour, not customer satisfaction that was never recorded.

